> **Important:**  
> - The actual `RootObjectMapper` instance (`rootObjectMapper`) must already contain the default settings you want to serialize (dynamic date formats, dynamic templates, date detection, numeric detection).  
> - The helper simply writes whatever is currently stored in that mapper into the supplied `XContentBuilder`.  
> - If you need to set those defaults programmatically, you would normally do so via the `RootObjectMapper.Builder` before building the mapper, e.g.:

```java
RootObjectMapper rootObjectMapper = new RootObjectMapper.Builder()
        .setDynamicDateFormats(/* ... */)
        .setDynamicTemplates(/* ... */)
        .setDetectDates(true)
        .setNumericDetection(true)
        .build();
```

Once the mapper is built, the snippet above will serialize it—including those defaults—into the `xContentBuilderInstance`, omitting any runtime fields.

